WAIT — I know! **`server.on('upgrade')` was registered at createServer; but look at START(): `server.listen(p, cb)` — listen(0) — the OS picks the port. `hal.start(0)` RESOLVES in the listen callback. THEN the test calls open()...

But WHO could 404 a request BEFORE our upgrade listener? **`http.createServer(options.app)` — THE FAKE APP! If the upgrade event fired when NO 'upgrade' listener exists... we always have one. Hmm.

**UNLESS THE REQUEST ISN'T AN UPGRADE**: Node routes Connection:Upgrade requests to 'upgrade' listeners ONLY when the request is well-formed (Upgrade header + Connection: upgrade + method GET). If the CLIENT-side headers are malformed, Node treats it as a NORMAL request → hands to the fake app → `(req, res) => undefined` → NO RESPONSE → the client hangs (not 404).

So who WROTE "HTTP/1.1 404"?! Let me look at the full debug log around t=...58427 to see WHICH engine (port) answered and what preceded: engineStart of 56690, wssClose events, drain times. Especially: **was there an engine restart** — i.e., did the port get reassigned mid-suite?

